      en: ["The studio opened its doors in 1977 near Cable Beach on New Providence Island.", "AC/DC's 'Back in Black,' the second best-selling album of all time, was recorded here in 1980.", "Chris Blackwell intended the studio to be a remote 'musical colony' for his artists.", "The house band popularized a unique blend of Caribbean reggae and European electronics.", "Iron Maiden recorded three consecutive albums at the studio during the mid-1980s.", "Operations were permanently ceased in September 2010 following increasing local instability."],
